            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This paper describes the long-term effect of conservative, interventional and surgical treatment in coronary heart disease on the prognosis and on the quality of life. It is difficult to decide if prognosis or quality of life is more influenced by the different therapeutic measures.</AbstractText>
